# =====================================================
# LOCK FILES
# =====================================================
#
# Lockfiles are COMMITTED on purpose. Ignoring them means every clone
# and every CI build re-resolves dependencies, so the tree that ships
# is not the tree that was tested — which is how the autumn-js/next@16
# peer conflict reached production unnoticed.
#
# tss-website/package-lock.json was already tracked (gitignore does not
# apply to tracked files), so only guidon/ was actually affected.
#
# Deterministic installs are also a hard requirement for self-hosting
# Guidon — see TODO.md §13 (migrations/deploy) and §15 (upgrades).

# yarn — not used in this repo; kept ignored to avoid stray lockfiles
yarn.lock
yarn-error.log

# pnpm
pnpm-lock.yaml

# bun
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# pnpm
pnpm-lock.yaml

# =====================================================
# DEBUG & TEST FILES
# =====================================================

coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.test.js
*.spec.js

# =====================================================
# DOCS
# =====================================================
#
# `docs/` was ignored wholesale, which silently discarded every document
# written into it. TODO.md §26 requires exactly the opposite — self-hosting,
# configuration, upgrade, backup and architecture guides all live in docs/
# and must ship with the repository.
#
# Only generated output is ignored now.

docs/**/_generated/
docs/**/*.tmp.md

# =====================================================
# DATABASE
# =====================================================

# Supabase
db.sqlite
*.db

# =====================================================
# MEDIA FILES
# =====================================================

# Backgrounds folder (keep assets if needed)
!assets/discord/backgrounds/*
assets/discord/*.png
assets/discord/*.jpg
assets/discord/*.gif
assets/discord/*.svg

